v1d (candidate -- gate hardened; full-40 x2-budget validation pending)

v1 = v0 rewritten for legibility: one insertion algorithm, one prefilter
semantic, zero dead knobs. Kernel 2199 -> 1567 lines, API 29 -> 19 methods.

Deliberate behavior changes vs v0 (everything else is deletion):
  1. The seeder now uses the same insertion path as the anneal. v0's seeder
     ran a second, older algorithm because reconstructOrdered never inherited
     the eventLocal flag -- measured an accident, not a design (seed A/B over
     all 40: 18W/11T/11L, mean -2.16% in favour of the unified path).
  2. Area prefilter uses min-over-orientations bbox area (v0 used orient 0's,
     the largest for 8% of blocks -> could reject a bay a slimmer orientation
     fits).
  3. The dense fallback uses the same sound same-layer prefilter as every
     other scan (v0 used a j>=l variant there that over-rejects legal layered
     placements; measured near-noise when swapped, KERNEL_SPEC sec 179).
  4. Phase-3 fallback gained the area screen; portfolio threads re-evaluate
     their post-compaction solution before the global-best merge (v0 compared
     pre-compaction bests).

Lineage: v0 = offline campaign end point ("smax78-v82"), tagged v0 in git.
Old-numbering (v57-v85) references live in docs/KERNEL_SPEC.md.

v1d adds the gate repair program (the two-budget T900 verdict exposed it):
  - retime_block kernel primitive: shift/extend a stay in time, vp-gated.
  - gate ladder reordered least-destructive first: nudges -> retimes
    (entry +1 / exit +1: time sidesteps exact-touch artifacts at <= a few
    tardy days) -> relocations (tight before loose).
  - deadline-aware: every rescue stage checks that another checker call fits.
  - portfolio reserves gate budget (3 + 0.03n s, cap 15).
  - fallback ladder gains a SEED FLOOR before _trivial (~1000x better floor).
  - OGC_DIAG=1 emits stderr gate/fallback events (harness logs them; the
    grading server never sets it).
